	(564, 'christies', 4889324, 'https://www.christies.com/en/lot/lot-4889324?ldp_breadcrumb=back', 9, 5, '54', 'sold', 'A POLISH SASH, LATE 18TH, EARLY 19TH CENTURY', 'GBP 1,440', 'GBP 600 - GBP 800', 1, 'A POLISH SASH, LATE 18TH, EARLY 19TH CENTURY\nwoven with pink,blue and white stripes terminating in a rosette border--\n119in. x 23in. (285cm. x 55cm.)\n; a Safavid sash fragment with one partial end panel with salmon pink flowering shrubs beneath beige, green and pink floral stripes--6.5in. x 42in. (16cm. x 101cm.); and half a Polish sash, woven with the letters S F in the corners--\n141in. x 6in. (340cm. x 14cm.)\n; and another Polish sash, the yellow ground woven with floral stripes, the ends with Persian style flowering carnation shrubs, woven with the initials MK JK in each corner with cyrillic equivalent, probably for Kniazia Jusupova in the village of Kupavno near Bogorodsk, Russia, active 1803-1833--25in. x 100in. (32cm. x 256cm.) (4)', '', 'ok', '2026-10-17 06:52:00', '2026-10-17 06:52:00', '2026-10-17 06:52:00'),
	(565, 'christies', 4889325, 'https://www.christies.com/en/lot/lot-4889325?ldp_breadcrumb=back', 9, 5, '55', 'sold', 'A VELVET PRAYER HANGING, PERSIAN, CIRCA 1900', 'GBP 600', 'GBP 700 - GBP 800', 1, 'A VELVET PRAYER HANGING, PERSIAN, CIRCA 1900\nwoven with a pair of stylised cypress trees, each flanked by birds beneath an arched niche, the lateral borders with a row of brightly coloured ogival medallions, with inscription woven to the lower edge--\n71 x 46½in. (180 x 118cm.);\na prayer-hanging of silk ikat, woven with a stylised cypress tree flanked by peacocks beneath a polychrome\nmehrab\n, within striped borders, backed with printed cotton--\nPersian, circa 1900\n; and a silk panel woven with zigzag bands of cypress trees (worn)--17in. x 24in. (43cm. x 61cm.) (3)', 'See Persische Seiden, Krefeld, 1988, cat 72, page 50 for a very similar silk to the third described here.', 'ok', '2026-10-17 06:52:04', '2026-10-17 06:52:04', '2026-10-17 06:52:04'),
	(566, 'christies', 4889328, 'https://www.christies.com/en/lot/lot-4889328?ldp_breadcrumb=back', 9, 5, '58', 'sold', 'TWO DERVISH HATS', 'GBP 120', 'GBP 400 - GBP 600', 0, 'TWO DERVISH HATS\nthe first a domed white felt cap covered with blue cotton, embroidered with geometric patterns, with a glass ferrule; and the second covered with red embroidery\nBoth late 20th century', 'The first cap is worn by masters of the Khaksar dervishes. See: Richard Gramlish, \'Die Shiitischen Derwischorden Persiens III (Wiesbaden 1981), p5. The red cap with gul-style decoration is typical of the Cerrahiye Halvetiye, and is generally worn with a green sash. See: N Atasoy, \'Dervis Ceyizi,\' (Istanbul 2000), p.84.', 'ok', '2026-10-17 06:52:07', '2026-10-17 06:52:07', '2026-10-17 06:52:07'),
