	(573, 'christies', 4889339, 'https://www.christies.com/en/lot/lot-4889339?ldp_breadcrumb=back', 9, 5, '69', 'sold', 'A MAGNIFICENT BOKHARAN NOBLEMAN\'S ROBE, 19TH CENTURY', 'GBP 13,200', 'GBP 4,000 - GBP 6,000', 1, 'A MAGNIFICENT BOKHARAN NOBLEMAN\'S ROBE, 19TH CENTURY\nthe multi-coloured velvet ground embroidered in gilt strip with stellar medallions, lined with silk ikat and trimmed with needlebraid\nSee Back Cover Illustration', 'This lot is sold with an original invoice from D Arditti & Co, Tangier, showing its purchase in 1932 for GBP35. This is a particularly splendid example of a Khan\'s robe of superb quality and preservation. See Pip Rau, Ikat, for discussion of the use of robes in Bokharan society of the 19th century.', 'ok', '2026-10-17 06:52:38', '2026-10-17 06:52:38', '2026-10-17 06:52:38'),
