	(701, 'christies', 4684308, 'https://www.christies.com/en/lot/lot-4684308?ldp_breadcrumb=back', 10, 6, '94', 'sold', 'A PANEL OF RED SILK, OTTOMAN, 17TH CENTURY', 'GBP 1,320', 'GBP 700 - GBP 1,000', 0, 'A PANEL OF RED SILK, OTTOMAN, 17TH CENTURY\nwoven in silks and metal thread with five columns of meandering stems bearing artichoke palemttes, with tulips and carnations between--\n43½ x 20½in. (110 x 52cm.), metal thread worn\n; and a panel of green satin woven in silks and metal threads with an ogival lattice enclosing red ground tulip and carnation medallions--\n55 in. x 26in. (140cm. x 66cm.), also Ottoman, 17th century, joined and wo rn', '', 'ok', '2026-10-17 07:04:29', '2026-10-17 07:04:29', '2026-10-17 07:04:29'),
